\subsection*{Bare ground cover}

Analyses of bare ground were conducted as cover classes via cumulative link models\footnote{Bareground was also assessed as approximate proportions by transforming cover classes into proportions at the subplot level via hurdle models see Appendix.}). While other cover classes on the fan appear to be stable it is evident that bare ground appeared to be disappearing regardless of metric (Figure \ref{fig:barecoverclass}, \ref{fig:bare} \& \ref{fig:bgcover}). The top-ranked model was \emph{as.factor(Year) + (1 | Plot) + (1 | SubplotID)} (AICc weight = 0.73). The predictions from this model (Appendix Figure \ref{fig:barepred}) closely align with those observed (Figure \ref{fig:barecoverclass}). The second-ranked model replicated the variables first but with the inclusion of distance from fence, and indicated bare ground increased with distance from the fence. The support for the \emph{Year} variable as a factor rather than a continuous variable suggests that  factors determining bare ground coverage is more complicated than a time bound trajectory.


