\emph{Gingidia enysii} has only been found on two transects (once on in a single subplot on R10 and in five subplots on RR3). Modelling was restricted to RR3 (hence no plot random effect was included) and limited to null model, a year effect, and a year as factor effect. The top-ranked model (\emph{1 + (1|Subplot)}) suggested the presence of \emph{G. enysii} was best explained as a simple average(AIC weight = 0.68), while the second-ranked model (\emph{Year  + (1|Subplot)}  suggested that the cover class of the species was increasing year on year (AIC weight = 0.26) likely due to a proliferation at a single subplot (RR3 subplot 960).


